<title>PORTUGAL: GEC-Alsthom set for Portugese contract - papers.</title>
<headline>GEC-Alsthom set for Portugese contract - papers.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC-Alsthom looks close to winning a government contract to provide trains for a new rail link across Lisbon's Tagus road bridge, Portuguese newspapers reported.</p>
<p>The daily Publico said GEC-Alsthom's proposal had come top in a first evaluation, ahead of bids by Germany's Siemens . It said the GEC-Alsthom cost estimate had been the lowest.</p>
<p>GEC-Alsthom has made a proposal to provide eight four-carriage double-decker trains for 21 billion escudos and another to provide single deck trains for 19.4 billion.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
